  "jobTitle": "Principal Software Engineer",
  "summary": "Stephen Kelly is a results-driven Principal Software Engineer with a proven track record in embedded systems, industrial automation, and enterprise applications. He excels in modernizing legacy software, streamlining manufacturing workflows, and implementing scalable reporting solutions. With expertise in .NET development, SQL Server engineering, and embedded HMI design, Stephen is adept at leading cross-functional teams and driving technical innovation in high-demand environments.\n\n- Software Development & Architecture – Designing, developing, and modernizing applications across embedded systems, industrial automation, and enterprise solutions.\n\n- Legacy System Modernization – Migrating outdated applications (VB6, Access, .NET 1.1) to modern frameworks to enhance security, performance, and compatibility.\n\n- Database Engineering & Reporting – Expertise in SQL Server (2000–2019), ReportViewer, and T-SQL for data visualization and robust reporting solutions.\n\n- System Integration & Automation – Implementing BizTalk upgrades, EDI automation, and secure SFTP protocols to streamline ordering workflows.\n\n- Embedded Systems & HMI Development – Creating human-machine interfaces (HMI) for production equipment, integrating SQL Express for real-time monitoring.\n\n\n\n\n\nList of the operating systems:\n\n- Windows & Embedded Windows NT – Used for enterprise applications and embedded systems development. \n\n- Nucleus RTOS &VxWorks – Real-time operating systems for embedded and industrial automation solutions.\n\n- Linux – Utilized for development environments, system integration, and scripting tasks.\n\n- OpenVMS – Integrated within legacy enterprise systems, including interfacing with older applications and proprietary solutions.\n\n- Legacy UNIX Platforms – Experience across various UNIX-based systems, supporting software development, system maintenance, and interoperability between legacy applications.\n\n- Protocols and Technologies - Implemented a wide variety of protocols and APIs.  ",
